  "details": "On a fresh project I am getting the following error in the Omnisharp output log when I Open C# Project into VSCode.\nC:\\Program Files\\dotnet\\sdk\\6.0.400\\Microsoft.Common.CurrentVersion.targets(2302,5): Error: The primary reference \"com.vrchat.core.vpm-resolver.Editor\" could not be resolved because it has an indirect dependency on the assembly \"Serilog.Sinks.Unity3D, Version=1.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null\" which was built against the \".NETFramework,Version=v4.7.2\" framework. This is a higher version than the currently targeted framework \".NETFramework,Version=v4.7.1\".\nCurrently the only way I could figure out how to fix this is by going into `Library\\PackageCache\\com.unity.ide.vscode@1.2.3\\Editor\\ProjectGeneration\\ProjectGeneration.cs`, search for the `TargetFrameworkVersion` variable and manually change it to `v4.7.2`.\nI also checked the project gen for unity's VisualStudio package and it had the same hardcoded v4.7.1 as well.\nIs there a proper way to make it so I don't have to update that file for every VCC project I make?",
